A developer writes the following Android `Service` to download a 50 MB exam package:

```java
public class ExamDownloadService extends Service {
    @Override
    public int onStartCommand(Intent intent, int flags, int startId) {
        // Performs synchronous 30-second HTTP file download directly here
        downloadLargeExamPackageSynchronously();
        return START_STICKY;
    }
    @Override
    public IBinder onBind(Intent intent) { return null; }
}
```

What happens when an Activity starts `ExamDownloadService` and the user tries to scroll the UI?

Compare the two ways of saving a user's dark-mode preference using Android `SharedPreferences.Editor`:

```java
SharedPreferences prefs = getSharedPreferences("user_settings", MODE_PRIVATE);
SharedPreferences.Editor editor = prefs.edit();
editor.putBoolean("DARK_MODE", true);

// Option 1: editor.commit();
// Option 2: editor.apply();
```

Why is `editor.apply()` generally recommended over `editor.commit()` when called on the UI thread?

A developer subclasses `SQLiteOpenHelper` to manage an offline exam database on Android:

```java
public class ExamDbHelper extends SQLiteOpenHelper {
    public static final int DATABASE_VERSION = 2;
    public static final String DATABASE_NAME = "exit_exam.db";

    public ExamDbHelper(Context context) {
        super(context, DATABASE_NAME, null, DATABASE_VERSION);
    }
    @Override
    public void onCreate(SQLiteDatabase db) { /* creates tables */ }
    @Override
    public void onUpgrade(SQLiteDatabase db, int oldVersion, int newVersion) { /* alters tables */ }
}
```

If a user already has version `1` of `exit_exam.db` installed on their phone and updates the app (where `DATABASE_VERSION` is now `2`), when and how is `onUpgrade()` triggered?
